from pathlib import Path
import json,hashlib
import pandas as pd,numpy as np
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
S=pd.read_csv(P/'diagnostic_summary.csv');C=pd.read_csv(P/'reference_C.csv');A=pd.read_csv(P/'cohort_abilities.csv');R=pd.read_csv(P/'finish_cohort_rewards.csv');O=pd.read_csv(P/'training_oracle_parameters.csv')
def table(d):
 def f(x):return f'{x:.6f}' if isinstance(x,(float,np.floating)) else str(x)
 return '| '+' | '.join(d.columns)+' |\n| '+' | '.join(['---']*len(d.columns))+' |\n'+'\n'.join('| '+' | '.join(f(x) for x in row)+' |' for row in d.itertuples(index=False,name=None))+'\n'
def write(name,text):
 (P/(name+'.md')).write_text('# '+name.replace('_',' ').capitalize()+'\n\n'+text+'\n\nDiagnostic only. No constants selected, replacement model trained, frozen definitions changed, prospective outcomes accessed or promotion authorized.\n')
def rows(group,labels):return S[S.group.eq(group)&S.diagnostic.isin(labels)]
labels=['primary','return_half','return_double','oracle_occupancy','oracle_attempts','oracle_conversion_pool','oracle_combined']
write('HAZARD_ACCOUNTING','Exact reward integral: I=integral exp(Tt)dt over 0–5 minutes, where T is the transient S/GA/GB generator. The first row of I is weighted by successive round-survival mass. Action counts are occupancy times Poisson action rates; terminal counts are occupancy times absorbing hazards. Returns exclude mandatory round-end resets. Ever-entry tracks first entry before standing KO and round expiration.\n\n'+table(rows('ALL',labels)[['diagnostic','ever_entry','entries','ground_minutes','ground_share','returns','sub_attempts','ground_actions','sub_finishes','ground_ko','standing_ko']])+'\nRaw finish rewards belong to the CTMC. Composed conditional probabilities renormalize KO/SUB, then multiply by unchanged external MOV0 F. Do not equate raw SUB 0.100154 with composed SUB 0.127442. All-fight distributions, all nine years, and every fight are saved in reward_distributions.csv, annual_rewards.csv and the record archive. Exact reward closure and baseline reproduction pass.\n\n'+table(R))
write('GROUND_ENTRY_DIAGNOSTIC','Primary ever-entry mean is 0.816715, but this is a model expectation, not measured frequency. Training homogeneous population entries/alive-minute average '+f'{O.modeled_entries_per_alive_min.mean():.6f}'+', versus successful-TD proxy '+f'{O.training_TD_landed_per_fight_min.mean():.6f}'+'. These are equally weighted division-year diagnostics, not fight-weighted estimates. A TD is not necessarily an independent new ground episode.\n\nAccess remains frozen TD attempts/total elapsed minute. Entry applies it only in S, multiplying by geometric attacker-success/opponent-resistance. This introduces standing-opportunity gating absent from its denominator. Successful TD count per fight-minute is already reduced by standing availability in the historical measurement. Applying it only during simulated S reduces action mass again. Ground via guard pulls and knockdowns is omitted; magnitude unidentifiable.\n\n'+table(rows('ALL',[f'entry_{f:g}' for f in [.5,.75,1,1.25,1.5,2]])[['diagnostic','ever_entry','entries','ground_minutes','sub_attempts','full_SUB','LL','Brier']]))
write('GROUND_OCCUPANCY_DIAGNOSTIC','Observed input is decision-only generic CTRL, not total ground time. For symmetric population q, entry e=access*TD-success and return=e*(1-q)/q. The bilateral generator has stationary ground share 2q/(1+q), not 2q. Actor occupancy q/(1+q) is below q; multiplying conditional work s/q by occupancy reconstructs s/(1+q) even before resets and absorbing finishes.\n\nTraining finite-horizon population ground-share mean is '+f'{O.modeled_ground_share.mean():.6f}'+', against CTRL target '+f'{O.target_CTRL_share.mean():.6f}'+'. '+str(int((~O.occupancy_target_attainable).sum()))+'/117 division-year targets cannot be reached even at effectively zero return. Entry scarcity, round reset and finish absorption constrain this proxy oracle. It is not evidence CTRL equals ground truth.\n\n'+table(rows('ALL',['primary','return_half','oracle_occupancy'])[['diagnostic','ground_minutes','ground_share','sub_attempts','full_SUB','LL','Brier']])+'\nCTRL may include clinch, omits neutral/bottom activity and scramble duration, and the decision-only sample differs from all-history activity. Those mismatches cannot be numerically corrected without a measurement contract. Inflated control denominators can lower conditional SUB work; changing decision selection can bias either direction.')
write('RETURN_TO_STANDING_DIAGNOSTIC','The frozen proxy is own access*own TD conversion*(1-directional CTRL share)/directional CTRL share. It is not measured escape. Its occupancy inversion assumes a single ground state and own successful access, whereas entry uses a different matchup-adjusted rate and the chain contains two actor states. This is an algebraic inconsistency, not an inferred escape deficiency.\n\nHalf return increases ground minutes 2.382161→2.953228 and attempts 0.353351→0.438922. Full SUB increases 12.7442%→14.8240%, recovering 41.97% of the observed mean deficit; LL recovers 74.77% of the Arm C gap but remains worse. No sensitivity is selected.\n\n'+table(rows('ALL',[f'return_{f:g}' for f in [.5,.75,1,1.25,1.5,2]])[['diagnostic','ground_minutes','returns','sub_attempts','full_SUB','LL','Brier']]))
write('SUBMISSION_CREATION_DIAGNOSTIC','Frozen creation is sqrt((A SUB/min / clipped A decision CTRL share)*(B SUB-faced/min / clipped B decision CTRL-allowed share)). Thus it is incorrect to say the POC simply applies total-time SUB rate unchanged while grounded: it already divides by estimated control opportunity. The failure is consistency of reconstructed occupancy with that denominator, plus the meaning of CTRL and square-root pairing. The latter compresses attacker and opponent extremes and combines unrelated career exposures without fitting schedule-adjusted latent action effects.\n\nThe training-derived aggregate attempt correction factors span '+f'{O.attempt_factor.min():.6f}–{O.attempt_factor.max():.6f}'+', median '+f'{O.attempt_factor.median():.6f}'+'. The numerical proximity to 2 is descriptive; no paper constant was copied or chosen. Finite-horizon population expected attempts/alive-time fall short of twice the preserved total-time submission rate. The attempt oracle corrects this aggregate reward moment only; it cannot identify true submission-capable duration.\n\n'+table(rows('ALL',['primary','oracle_attempts','oracle_combined'])[['diagnostic','sub_attempts','sub_finishes','full_SUB','conditional_SUB','LL','Brier']])+'\nNo causally unique assignment between creation and conversion can come from loss curves: only their product enters Q. Sensitivities confirm exact equality of conditional probabilities at identical factors; action rewards distinguish event counts. There is no observed threat-quality or position-specific opportunity denominator.')
v=json.loads((P/'conversion_variance.json').read_text())
write('SUBMISSION_CONVERSION_DIAGNOSTIC','Conversion preserves coherent successes and recorded attempts; finishes with zero recorded attempts are excluded from conversion trials, not repaired. Attempt records are not independent threat trials. Of 8520 fighter sides, '+str(v['positive_denominator_sides'])+' have positive prior denominators. Median denominator 1; median effective support 1/51=0.019608. Fixed prior is 50 attempts; population/division means are training-only.\n\nWithin-division/year residual raw variance '+f"{v['raw_residual_variance']:.6f}"+' falls to '+f"{v['posterior_residual_variance']:.6f}"+'; removed fraction '+f"{v['variance_removed_fraction']:.6%}"+'. This is empirical variance compression on supported rows, not a posterior uncertainty calculation. Raw variance is strongly inflated by tiny supports. Weakening this prior was not tested as a replacement.\n\n'+table(rows('ALL',['primary','oracle_conversion_pool'])[['diagnostic','conversion_weighted','full_SUB','LL','Brier']])+'\nThe original pooled-conversion ablation LL 0.628936 versus identity0.627949 shows only a small fighter-conversion contribution. Training aggregate replacement LL 0.625456 recovers 12.36% of the Arm C LL gap and 3.07% of mean SUB deficit; this is far less than opportunity checks. Broad compression alone does not support classification C. Raw supports, priors, coherent trial counts and posterior distribution are saved.')
write('GROUND_STRIKING_DIAGNOSTIC','GnP work uses significant-ground attempts/total-time divided by the same clipped CTRL proxies. Ground KO conversion is a pooled latent allocation of KO wins in proportion to significant ground/total attempts. It is not observed location or individual damage conversion; no strike-landing/head-target stages exist. This assumption competes with SUB within GA/GB, and longer ground persistence increases both hazards.\n\n'+table(rows('ALL',[f'strike_{f:g}' for f in [.5,.75,1,1.25,1.5,2]])[['diagnostic','ground_actions','ground_ko','sub_finishes','full_SUB','LL','Brier']])+'\nPrimary raw ground KO0.041359 is substantially smaller than standing KO0.249948. Broad submission undercount cannot be explained simply by assigning all KO through GnP. The curve measures sensitivity, not verified ground-KO attribution.')
write('ORACLE_STAGE_DIAGNOSTICS','Training-only January-1 division aggregates set each isolated oracle. Occupancy uses best available generic CTRL proxy; attempts match historical aggregate SUB activity per alive minute in a homogeneous training population chain; conversion uses unshrunk coherent training success/attempt ratio; combined changes creation/conversion while leaving entry/return fixed. All use target-independent division/year factors. Future and target outcomes do not enter parameter construction. These are proxy oracles, not omniscient states.\n\n'+table(rows('ALL',labels)[['diagnostic','LL','Brier','multiclass_LL','summed_Brier','full_SUB','conditional_SUB','ground_minutes','sub_attempts']])+'\nAttempt and occupancy checks recover respectively 95.30% and 85.00% of the LL gap. Both still fail Arm C; combined LL 0.608541 also fails. Mean SUB matching does not guarantee individual calibration. Occupancy oracle fails its target in 112/117 contexts; favorable performance cannot validate its physical meaning. Combined is the sole preregistered two-stage diagnostic, not a combination search.')
write('HAZARD_SENSITIVITY_CURVES','Five independent six-point sweeps; factor1 reproduces primary. No combinations or winner. Conversion scaling is terminal hazard scaling and must not be read as a new calibrated probability. Attempt and conversion terminal curves overlap exactly; nonconverting attempts differ. All subgroup/annual metrics are in diagnostic_summary.csv.\n\n![Overall responses](sensitivity.png)\n\n![Frozen B3/B5 responses](B3_B5_sensitivity.png)\n\n'+table(S[S.group.eq('ALL')&~S.diagnostic.str.startswith('oracle')][['diagnostic','LL','Brier','full_SUB','conditional_SUB']]))
for cell in ['B3','B5']:
 primary=rows(cell,['primary']).iloc[0];half=rows(cell,['return_half']).iloc[0];gap=primary.observed_conditional_SUB-primary.conditional_SUB;recover=(half.conditional_SUB-primary.conditional_SUB)/gap
 text='Membership and observed finish cohort unchanged. '+f'Primary SUB {primary.conditional_SUB:.6%}, observed {primary.observed_conditional_SUB:.6%}; deficit {gap:.6%}. Half return recovers {recover:.2%} of that mean deficit.'+'\n\n'+table(rows(cell,labels)[['diagnostic','LL','Brier','conditional_SUB','entries','ground_minutes','sub_attempts','ground_ko','standing_ko']])+'\nFinish-only reward comparison against the aggregate finish cohort:\n\n'+table(R[R.group.isin(['ALL_FINISH',cell])])+'\nFighter-side directional input comparison:\n\n'+table(A[A.group.eq(cell)][['ability','mean','mean_prior','mean_effective_support','median_den']])
 if cell=='B3':text+='\nB3 has more entries and more SUB creation than aggregate, so the identity signal reaches the engine. However, realized opportunity is too short to express its submission work fully. Entry-only deficiency is insufficient: B3 ever entry is already 0.888471 and expected entries 2.503558 in finishes. Occupancy and attempt oracles improve B3 LL beyond its Arm C0.702832, but neither reaches observed SUB share. Conversion pooling adds little. Standing KO remains a large competing reward. These isolated responses are nonadditive and cannot partition an observed outcome deficit causally.'
 else:text+='\nB5 creation is stronger than aggregate, and input submission/allowed-work rates retain pressure-vulnerability alignment before conversion. The signal is compressed by square-root construction and scarce conversion support, not wholly erased: identity predicts SUB39.58% versus population31.85%. Occupancy and attempt checks bring SUB near51–52%, with LL improvements. Training pooled conversion alone slightly worsens B5 LL, rejecting a simple conversion-only explanation. Ground KO is small relative to standing KO. There is no defensible additive causal decomposition of the observed deficit.'
 write(cell+'_ROOT_CAUSE',text)
write('STRIKING_PATHWAY_DAMAGE','Standing hazard is independently computed from geometric KO creation/vulnerability and KD creation/vulnerability, multiplied by latent non-ground fraction and population-control normalization. It is not the saved Arm C striking probability. The engine already overallocates KO relative to observed submissions: full KO34.58% versus31.95% actual. A1/A4 failure is not explained by excessive SUB stealing KO; their primary SUB means are too low.\n\n'+table(S[S.group.isin(['A1','A2','A4'])&S.diagnostic.isin(['primary','return_half','oracle_occupancy','oracle_attempts','oracle_combined'])][['diagnostic','group','LL','Brier','conditional_SUB','ground_ko','standing_ko']])+'\nA1/A4 improve under opportunity diagnostics, while A2 damage appears: attempt oracle LL 0.360857 exceeds Arm C0.348743; combined0.368687. Therefore a global opportunity correction is not a finished solution. External MOV0 F and decision probability are unchanged in every diagnostic. Damage arises in conditional KO/SUB allocation and standing/ground competition, not a changed finish model.')
annual=S[S.diagnostic.eq('primary')&S.group.isin([str(y) for y in range(2018,2027)])].merge(C[['group','LL']],on='group',suffixes=('','_C'));annual['LL_delta']=annual.LL-annual.LL_C
write('ANNUAL_HAZARD_FAILURE',table(annual[['group','n_finish','LL','LL_C','LL_delta','ground_minutes','sub_attempts','full_SUB','observed_SUB']])+'\nOnly 2021 improves versus Arm C. Ground minutes remain roughly 2.33–2.44 across years while expected SUB attempts decline from 0.376 to 0.326. Underproduction persists in every year, so no sole modern-era cutoff explains it. Annual support/missingness evidence is in annual_support_coverage.csv: measured missingness and support are reported separately, with no inference of historically available publication vintages. The sealed corpus ends 2026-08-15. No year excluded; partial 2026 retained. Stable structural opportunity inconsistency exists in all folds, but source era and changing opponents cannot be causally separated by these descriptive aggregates.')
support=S[S.diagnostic.eq('primary')&S.group.str.startswith('support')].merge(C[['group','LL']],on='group',suffixes=('','_C'));support['LL_delta']=support.LL-support.LL_C
write('SUPPORT_LEVEL_DIAGNOSTIC','Strata use the lower prior-fight count of the two fighters: debut0; low1–2; moderate3–7; high8+. They are descriptive, not adjusted causal contrasts.\n\n'+table(support[['group','n','n_finish','LL','LL_C','LL_delta','conditional_SUB','sub_attempts','ground_minutes']])+'\nAbility-specific denominators and decision counts remain necessary: many fights do not guarantee submission conversion trials. Mean conversion support is4.48% attacker and3.42% defender. Higher history cannot fix a mismatched state exposure denominator. These results do not establish that weakening support priors would improve predictions.')
components=[('ground access','prior TD attempts/elapsed','entry per standing minute','access*sqrt(success*opponent failure complement)','observed numerator; wrong opportunity semantics','downward realized entries','high'),('ground occupancy','decision CTRL share','actor state minutes','bilateral CTMC with clipped geometric CTRL','proxy; no true ground target','shortfall against proxy','highest'),('control retention','decision CTRL and access','episode duration','stationary inverse','assumption; distinct rates for entry/return','inconsistent occupancy','highest'),('return-to-standing','no escape observation','state exit hazard','own access*conversion*(1-q)/q','estimated proxy only','too rapid relative proxy','highest'),('submission work','all-history attempts/elapsed','attempts/ground minute','sqrt(work/own CTRL * faced/allowed CTRL)','observed counts; denominator mismatch','under-reconstructed aggregate activity','highest'),('submission conversion','coherent successes/attempts','threat conversion','50-attempt shrink then geometric pairing','tiny denominators; missing zero-attempt wins','extreme compression; not main mean deficit','medium'),('GnP activity','significant ground attempts/elapsed','actions/ground minute','same CTRL normalization','no bottom/action quality','opportunity undercount; noisier','medium'),('ground KO hazard','KO labels plus strike shares','KO/action','latent equal-attempt allocation pooled','finish location not observed','unknown','medium'),('standing KO hazard','KO/KD rates and vulnerability','KO/standing minute','geometric rates and latent ground subtraction','governed inputs; new mechanistic map','too much relative SUB in A1/A4','high')]
m=pd.DataFrame(components,columns=['Component','UFC EDGE measurement','Required quantity','Current mapping','Evidence quality','Likely bias','Priority']);m['Holmes treatment']='See corresponding row in HOLMES_UFC_EDGE_COMPONENT_COMPARISON.md'
write('MEASUREMENT_TO_HAZARD_MATRIX',table(m)+'\nDirectionality: entry, control, creation, conversion and GnP all include opponent histories; standing KO does too. It would be incorrect to call the entire simulator one-sided. Opponent SUB-creation multiplier median0.9892, interquartile0.7025–1.3221, 5th–95th0.4090–2.1608. Conversion defense support is only3.42% on average; ground KO conversion is population-level; return has no separate escape effect. These are allowed-behavior modifiers, not opponent-adjusted latent skills. Exactly one of the five ground mechanisms has no independently measured defender state: return/escape; pooled ground KO conversion also lacks personal finishing resistance. No causal fraction of accuracy attributable to missing defense is identifiable.')
write('NEXT_POC_DECISION','Primary classification **E — MULTIPLE MEASUREMENT-TO-HAZARD ERRORS ARE MATERIAL**, centered on coupled opportunity/entry/persistence mapping. The total-time access gate, unilateral occupancy inversion embedded in a bilateral reset chain, and CTRL-conditioned work reconstruction do not conserve observed activity exposure. Favorable occupancy and attempt diagnostics establish recovery potential; they do not uniquely identify true positional causes. A and B remain competing descriptions of the same coupled opportunity error, rather than independently proven physical causes. Conversion compression is real but not a primary aggregate explanation; missing escape and latent KO attribution remain limitations. Generic-ground architecture is not disproved (F unsupported).\n\nIdentity contributes: frozen identity-versus-population LL −0.021370, while primary-versus-Arm C +0.020172. This audit preserves both facts. No oracle beats Arm C overall, even when B3/B5 improve; A2 can deteriorate. Mean SUB calibration recovery is not a deployable result.\n\nA further POC is scientifically justified **only after** a specific training-only correction contract passes. Exact next milestone: **UFC_EDGE_GROUND_OPPORTUNITY_REWARD_CONSISTENCY_CONTRACT_V1**. Freeze a rule connecting total-time TD/SUB/GnP rates to mutually exclusive state opportunity; jointly account for both actor states, round resets and competing absorption; require training-only aggregate reward consistency and explicit infeasible-target handling. Separate generic CTRL from submission-capable ground opportunity and preserve missingness. Specify individual-loss/striking gates and unchanged baselines before any new outer evaluation. No numeric factor from this audit is recommended. If this contract cannot produce a defensible, predefinable exposure rule, do not run a second POC. No challenger is authorized or built here.\n\nValidation source_hashes and VALIDATION.json confirm unchanged PR163 records and exact baseline/half/double reproduction. The audit uses exact propagation, so Monte Carlo seeds/counts are irrelevant. Repeat-run verification and publication hashes accompany the manifest.')
write('README','Starting SHA 54a0b647825295b09342fa02cca4f40210bf4f94; audit branch audit/ground-pathway-measurement-hazard-v1. Read NEXT_POC_DECISION.md and MEASUREMENT_TO_HAZARD_MATRIX.md first.\n\nRegenerate: restore frozen PR163 records using its publication.py, then run audit.py, supplement.py, report.py. Original artifacts remain unchanged. All oracle parameters precede each outer year and are derived from frozen training totals. Protocol commits850b1b4 and implementation6a91c6b precede diagnostic scoring; c8206d5 records training-only infeasible targets. Numerical bug fix casts metric labels to float; no scientific specification changed. Static curves and complete machine tables accompany reports. Machine records may be packaged in DIAGNOSTIC_RECORDS.tar.xz parts; RECORDS_MANIFEST.json provides exact reconstruction/hash instructions.')
